--- /dev/null
+++ b/.claude/skills/spec-report/report.org
@@ -0,0 +1,115 @@
+#+TITLE: /spec-report report
+
+* status
+Implemented. Every requirement in the spec is carried out by
+=SKILL.md=, and nothing in the working copy contradicts the spec. The
+spec has no =conflict plan:= headings and none are needed. Nothing is
+left to plan. One example in the spec disagrees with its own naming
+rule; the skill follows the rule.
+
+* conflicts
+None. Each requirement below maps to a part of
+=.claude/skills/spec-report/SKILL.md= that does what the spec says,
+and no other file in the working copy writes or names a spec report.
+
+* conflict plans that can be removed
+None. The spec has no =conflict plan:= headings:
+
+: $ grep -n '^\*.*conflict plan:' .claude/skills/spec-report/spec.org
+: (no output)
+
+The only match for =conflict plan= is the requirement that defines
+the convention, at spec.org:30.
+
+* not implemented
+None.
+
+* implemented
+** R1. The artifacts: a skill in this dir, and the report (spec.org:3)
+- The skill is =.claude/skills/spec-report/SKILL.md=, added in
+  39d3485e "claude/skills/spec-report: Add the spec-report skill".
+- This report is the second artifact. It was produced by invoking the
+  skill as =/spec-report .claude/skills/spec-report/spec.org=, which
+  also shows the skill is installed and invocable as a command.
+
+** R2. disable-model-invocation (spec.org:4)
+=SKILL.md:8= sets =disable-model-invocation: true=.
+
+** R3. No hand-made report is committed (spec.org:6-8)
+Before this report, the working copy held no =report.org= in the
+skill's directory:
+
+: $ jj file list -r @ | grep spec-report
+: .claude/skills/spec-report/SKILL.md
+: .claude/skills/spec-report/spec.org
+
+The hand-written bootstrap report was posted to the list but never
+committed to this tree. This report replaces it, generated by the
+skill as spec.org:7-8 asks.
+
+** R4. Read the spec file given by args (spec.org:11-12)
+=SKILL.md:14-16= takes the path from =$ARGUMENTS=, and
+=SKILL.md:26-28= accepts exactly the four basenames the spec lists
+and stops on anything else or a missing file. =SKILL.md:58-59= has
+the whole spec read, with requirements numbered by line.
+
+** R5. Analyze the working copy using implementation and documentation (spec.org:13-15)
+=SKILL.md:77-83= judges the working copy "as checked out, not trunk"
+and defines the two kinds of evidence. =SKILL.md:90-95= asks for
+thoroughness: follow each requirement to the code, run read-only
+commands, and fan out read-only subagents for large specs.
+
+** R6. Notes are context, not implementation (spec.org:16-19)
+=SKILL.md:85-88= says notes are "context, never evidence that a
+requirement is met", and names =zib/= and text-only files such as
+=lore.org=, =research.org=, =todo.org=, and earlier reports.
+
+** R7. Use commit history for context (spec.org:20-21)
+=SKILL.md:66-73= reads =jj log= for the spec's directory and
+=jj log -p --git= for the spec, as context and evidence, while the
+working copy stays what is judged.
+
+** R8. Sibling report named by s/^spec/report/ (spec.org:22-25)
+=SKILL.md:30-40= derives the name with =sed=, and writes the report
+in the spec's format. Running that derivation on each spec form:
+
+: a/spec.org -> a/report.org
+: a/SPEC.md -> a/REPORT.md
+: a/spec--cli.org -> a/report--cli.org
+: a/SPEC--cli.md -> a/REPORT--cli.md
+
+spec.org:23 lists =REPORT--<name>.org= as an example, but the rule at
+spec.org:25 turns =SPEC--<name>.md= into =REPORT--<name>.md=. The
+skill follows the rule. The example at spec.org:23 could read
+=REPORT--<name>.md= to match.
+
+** R9. Report sections (spec.org:26-45)
+=SKILL.md:117-130= requires the sections in the spec's order:
+- concise summary status (spec.org:27): =SKILL.md:119-121=
+- conflicts, with whether a =conflict plan:= heading covers each
+  (spec.org:28-32): =SKILL.md:122-124=, with the heading convention at
+  =SKILL.md:61-64= and the check at =SKILL.md:100-102=
+- removable conflict plans (spec.org:33-34): =SKILL.md:105-106= and
+  =SKILL.md:125-127=
+- not implemented, "ready to implement" or "not ready to implement"
+  with questions (spec.org:35-40): =SKILL.md:108-113= and
+  =SKILL.md:128-129=
+- no plan in the report (spec.org:41-42): =SKILL.md:137-138=
+- implemented (spec.org:43): =SKILL.md:130=
+- evidence for all but the status (spec.org:44-45):
+  =SKILL.md:132-135=
+
+** R10. Commit the report, overwriting the existing one (spec.org:46-49)
+=SKILL.md:117= overwrites the report in full, and =SKILL.md:142-157=
+commits it alone, then checks the commit from the VCS state rather
+than from printed output, as the "Own the loop" section of
+=CLAUDE.md= asks.
+
+** R11. Move a sclr report.org aside (spec.org:50-52)
+=SKILL.md:44-54= moves =report.org= to =sclr-report.org= in its own
+preparatory commit when a sibling =lore.org= exists. This matches
+what sclr writes: =src/sclr/sclr:49= asks for =collab.org=,
+=lore.org=, and =report.org= in the spec's directory, and
+=src/sclr/sclr.1:72-73= documents =report.org= as "A concise account
+of the result". The skill's directory has no =lore.org=, so no move
+was needed for this report.
